      ],
      "category": {
        "_type": "localizedString",
        "de": "Streetfood",
        "en": "Street food"
      },
      "description": {
        "_type": "localizedPortableText",
        "de": [
          {
            "_key": "c9192ed538ad",
            "_type": "block",
            "children": [
              {
                "_key": "6a4cfbd3b50d",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": ["strong", "em"],
                "text": "Tteokbokki sind koreanische Reiskuchen in einer süß-scharfen Sauce. In Deutschland findest du Tteokbokki-Reiskuchen meist tiefgekühlt oder vakuumverpackt im Asia-Markt."
              }
            ],
            "level": 1,
            "listItem": "bullet",
            "markDefs": [],
            "style": "normal"
          },
          {
            "_key": "ff0ca8234237",
            "_type": "block",
            "children": [
              {
                "_key": "c8c1ae18ea33",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": "Das ist meine einfache Alltagsversion von Tteokbokki. In Korea gibt es viele verschiedene Arten von Tteokbokki – mit unterschiedlichen Saucen, Zutaten und Reiskuchen. Diese Version ist bewusst schlicht gehalten und funktioniert gut, wenn du zu Hause schnell etwas Warmes und Scharfes kochen möchtest."
              }
            ],
            "level": 1,
            "listItem": "bullet",
            "markDefs": [],
            "style": "normal"
          },
          {
            "_key": "1c9792a2a532",
            "_type": "block",
            "children": [
              {
                "_key": "3f85abcd3f1e",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": "Bei Tteokbokki gibt es verschiedene Arten von Reiskuchen. Reistteok ist meist etwas zäher, während Mil-tteok aus Weizenmehl oft weicher ist und die Sauce gut aufnimmt. In Korea haben viele Menschen ihre eigene Vorliebe dafür. Ich nehme in Deutschland meistens einfach die Sorte, die ich im Asia-Markt finde."
              }
            ],
            "level": 1,
            "listItem": "bullet",
            "markDefs": [],
            "style": "normal"
          },
          {
            "_key": "16f96214c442",
            "_type": "block",
            "children": [
              {
                "_key": "aada318a6989",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": "Tteokbokki-Reiskuchen findest du in Deutschland oft tiefgekühlt oder vakuumverpackt im Asia-Markt. Wenn sie gefroren sind, weiche ich sie vor dem Kochen kurz in Wasser ein, damit sie gleichmäßiger garen."
              }
            ],
            "level": 1,
            "listItem": "bullet",
            "markDefs": [],
            "style": "normal"
          },
          {
            "_key": "99553a8c5f5b",
            "_type": "block",
            "children": [
              {
                "_key": "0172b88a4058",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": "Eine kleine Sache ist bei koreanischen Rezepten wichtig: Der koreanische Esslöffel ist etwas kleiner als ein normaler deutscher Esslöffel. Viele koreanische Alltagsrezepte benutzen trotzdem Löffelangaben, weil es zu Hause praktisch ist. Ich versuche die Mengen hier so anzugeben, dass du das Rezept auch in Deutschland gut nachkochen kannst."
              }
            ],
            "level": 1,
            "listItem": "bullet",
            "markDefs": [],
            "style": "normal"
          },
          {
            "_key": "11367e88a308",
            "_type": "block",
            "children": [
              {
                "_key": "a534331f6e37",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "markDefs": [],
            "style": "normal"
          }
        ],
        "en": [
          {
            "_key": "246875214f74",
            "_type": "block",
            "children": [
              {
                "_key": "25c78d3e9ba9",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": "Tteokbokki is a Korean rice cake dish cooked in a sweet and spicy sauce. Tteokbokki rice cakes are usually sold frozen or vacuum-packed at Asian grocery stores or Korean online shops."
              }
            ],
            "level": 1,
            "listItem": "bullet",
            "markDefs": [],
            "style": "normal"
          },
          {
            "_key": "bbfa4ad8eafb",
            "_type": "block",
            "children": [
              {
                "_key": "db181bae167c",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": "This is my simple everyday version of tteokbokki. In Korea, there are many different varieties with different sauces, toppings, and types of rice cakes. This version is intentionally simple and works well when you want something warm, spicy, and quick at home."
              }
            ],
            "level": 1,
            "listItem": "bullet",
            "markDefs": [],
            "style": "normal"
          },
          {
            "_key": "5a13de35cb80",
            "_type": "block",
            "children": [
              {
                "_key": "b66ef2d6a7a3",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": "There are two common types of rice cakes for tteokbokki. Rice tteok is usually chewier, while mil-tteok, made with wheat flour, is often softer and absorbs the sauce well. Many people in Korea have their own preference, but either type works for this recipe."
              }
            ],
            "level": 1,
            "listItem": "bullet",
            "markDefs": [],
            "style": "normal"
          },
          {
            "_key": "0fabd09d6856",
            "_type": "block",
            "children": [
              {
                "_key": "dbf76eb96cd8",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": "If the rice cakes are frozen, soak them briefly in water before cooking so they soften and cook more evenly."
              }
            ],
            "level": 1,
            "listItem": "bullet",
            "markDefs": [],
            "style": "normal"
          },
          {
            "_key": "6a222074c24e",
            "_type": "block",
            "children": [
              {
                "_key": "907c9f736931",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": "Traditional Korean home recipes often use ordinary spoon measurements. For clarity, the quantities in this recipe are written so they are easy to follow with standard measuring spoons."
              }
            ],
            "level": 1,
            "listItem": "bullet",
            "markDefs": [],
            "style": "normal"
          },
          {
            "_key": "0f357f20f0b7",
            "_type": "block",
            "children": [
              {
                "_key": "497370672503",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "markDefs": [],
            "style": "normal"
          }
        ]
      },
