      "instructions": {
        "_type": "localizedPortableText",
        "de": [
          {
            "_key": "e6c7652357d8",
            "_type": "block",
            "children": [
              {
                "_key": "426b57bd9fe2",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": "Bringe 360 ml Wasser in einem Topf zum Kochen. Gib die Tteokbokki-Reiskuchen dazu. Wenn sie gefroren sind, weiche sie vorher kurz in Wasser ein."
              }
            ],
            "level": 1,
            "listItem": "number",
            "markDefs": [],
            "style": "normal"
          },
          {
            "_key": "40b2392ad867",
            "_type": "block",
            "children": [
              {
                "_key": "8e470354af35",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": "Wenn das Wasser wieder kocht, gib die Sauce-Zutaten dazu und verrühre alles gut. Rühre während des Kochens regelmäßig um, damit die Reiskuchen nicht am Topfboden kleben bleiben."
              }
            ],
            "level": 1,
            "listItem": "number",
            "markDefs": [],
            "style": "normal"
          },
          {
            "_key": "135935b32237",
            "_type": "block",
            "children": [
              {
                "_key": "0f543f655c22",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": "Köchele alles, bis die Sauce etwas eingekocht ist und leicht glänzt. Schneide die Lauchzwiebel mit einer Schere klein und streue Sesam darüber."
              }
            ],
            "level": 1,
            "listItem": "number",
            "markDefs": [],
            "style": "normal"
          },
          {
            "_key": "7b8b0ab3c445",
            "_type": "block",
            "children": [
              {
                "_key": "605c6f8cd235",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": "Sofort servieren. Wenn du die Tteokbokki sättigender machen möchtest, kannst du Eomuk, Kohl, gekochte Eier oder etwas mehr Sesam dazugeben."
              }
            ],
            "level": 1,
            "listItem": "number",
            "markDefs": [],
            "style": "normal"
          },
          {
            "_key": "c90980588bed",
            "_type": "block",
            "children": [
              {
                "_key": "403813bd5862",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "markDefs": [],
            "style": "normal"
          }
        ],
        "en": [
          {
            "_key": "23d25a3fba01",
            "_type": "block",
            "children": [
              {
                "_key": "7c4720cf7e0b",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": "Bring 360 ml of water to a boil in a pot. Add the tteokbokki rice cakes. If the rice cakes are frozen, soak them briefly in water first."
              }
            ],
            "level": 1,
            "listItem": "number",
            "markDefs": [],
            "style": "normal"
          },
          {
            "_key": "36e61fb1d6e8",
            "_type": "block",
            "children": [
              {
                "_key": "a69784d055c6",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": "When the water starts boiling again, add the sauce ingredients and mix well. Keep stirring often while the rice cakes cook, so they do not stick to the bottom."
              }
            ],
            "level": 1,
            "listItem": "number",
            "markDefs": [],
            "style": "normal"
          },
          {
            "_key": "17ebbb5dd412",
            "_type": "block",
            "children": [
              {
                "_key": "9014d3b2f672",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": "Simmer until the sauce has reduced and becomes slightly glossy. Cut the green onion into small pieces with scissors and sprinkle sesame seeds on top."
              }
            ],
            "level": 1,
            "listItem": "number",
            "markDefs": [],
            "style": "normal"
          },
          {
            "_key": "1228ac4c786d",
            "_type": "block",
            "children": [
              {
                "_key": "873826c968fc",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": "Serve right away. If you want to make it more filling, you can add eomuk, cabbage, boiled eggs, or extra sesame seeds."
              }
            ],
            "level": 1,
            "listItem": "number",
            "markDefs": [],
            "style": "normal"
          },
          {
            "_key": "0f790d91c9a6",
            "_type": "block",
            "children": [
              {
                "_key": "33b3c1f9cf5a",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "markDefs": [],
            "style": "normal"
          }
        ]
